              {
                "text": "**Analyzing the Data Structure**\n\nI'm now focusing on Example 1 to fully grasp how the \"frame\" and \"inside\" data are structured within these grids. Currently, I'm analyzing the row and column indices for the 3s frame, along with the coordinates and values of inner points. I'm aiming to create a mental model of this visual data to inform my next steps.\n\n\n**Mapping the Inner Dynamics**\n\nI've made a breakthrough! I've determined that clearing the frame points to zero initiates a 180-degree point reflection across the center, which I've confirmed with Example 1. This applies to the points inside the cleared frame. With Example 2, the behavior is more nuanced, specifically for center points, requiring further clarification for generalizations.\n\n\n**Investigating the Projection**\n\nI'm now diving deep into how inner points map to the output, specifically focusing on the idea of projection. In Example 1, I noticed a clear diagonal inversion of top-left to bottom-right. Example 2 shows some points going to all four frame corners, which has me stumped. I'm currently looking closely at Example 3, where the relationships between frame corners, their corresponding inner points, and the projected locations is now taking form.\n\n\n",
                "type": "reasoning_text"
              }
