              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n\n1. Locate the rectangular frame of a single non-zero color.\n2. The values inside the frame are mapped diagonally outward to the four external corners just beyond the frame:\n   - **Top-Left** inside value $\\rightarrow$ **Bottom-Right** outer corner $(r_{\\text{max}} + 1, c_{\\text{max}} + 1)$\n   - **Top-Right** inside value $\\rightarrow$ **Bottom-Left** outer corner $(r_{\\text{max}} + 1, c_{\\text{min}} - 1)$\n   - **Bottom-Left** inside value $\\rightarrow$ **Top-Right** outer corner $(r_{\\text{min}} - 1, c_{\\text{max}} + 1)$\n   - **Bottom-Right** inside value $\\rightarrow$ **Top-Left** outer corner $(r_{\\text{min}} - 1, c_{\\text{min}} - 1)$\n   *(If an inner dimension is 1, a single cell acts as both top/bottom and/or left/right).*\n3. The interior of the frame is cleared to 0.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid.",
